    heading(r'# xyno-crates.nvim'),
    blank,
    ...text(r'Your Rust file says rand::random::<u8>() and your Cargo.toml has never heard of rand. In most editors that is a red squiggle and a trip to a browser. Here it is a hint on the word, and one keystroke on the code-action menu: Add crate rand. Write #[derive(Serialize)] with serde added but its derive feature off, and rustc’s error does not tell you what to do; here the menu offers "Enable feature `derive` of `serde`" and edits Cargo.toml without touching your comments. Type Uuid::new_v4() with no uuid anywhere, and the import menu proposes uuid::Uuid, adds the crate, waits for rust-analyzer to load it and writes the use line. xyno-crates.nvim is the Cargo half of a Rust workflow in Neovim: three modules, about 3,370 lines of Lua, two sibling plugins underneath.'),
