    ...text(r'No global key is mapped by default. keymaps = true gives <leader>rA (:CrateAdd, in Rust and Cargo.toml buffers) and <leader>rG (the missing-feature fix for the diagnostics on the cursor line, in Rust buffers), both buffer-local; a table maps only what you list. vim.g.xyno_crate_check = false switches the hint off. Limits live in each module’s config table: debounce_ms 300, max_diagnostics 50, cargo_timeout_ms 180000, max_lines 20000 in crate_add; the scan caps (max_files, max_file_bytes and others) in crate_features; max_guesses 3, min_guess_len 3, poll_ms 1000, reload_timeout_ms 60000 in crate_import. The modules start once per session: a second setup() does not redefine their autocommands, language clients or keys.'),
    blank,
    ...sec(r'where it came from'),
    ...text(r'This is not a plugin that was designed in the abstract. In October 2026 xynovim, the author’s Neovim configuration for Rust, got a phase called "macros and dependencies". Its plan document (docs/PLAN_MACROS_DEPS.md) listed seven measured gaps in what rust-analyzer and the configuration did with derive macros, attributes, new dependencies, missing crate features and ambiguous imports. Three of them became this plugin: G3, a crate that is not yet a dependency cannot be imported (plan item 1.1, the unknown-crate check, and 3.3, import from crates that are not dependencies yet); G4, a missing crate feature is silent (item 1.3); and the :CrateAdd flow (item 1.2). On 2026-10-14 commit b9363cd added lua/config/crate_add.lua, crate_features.lua and crate_import.lua to xynovim (973, 2,018 and 282 lines, 3,273 in total) together with their specs. Two days of fixes followed (19f974c review fixes and b474307 field-test fixes on 2026-10-15, ff1c8fa portability on 2026-10-16). On 2026-10-22 the three files became xyno-crates.nvim in commit 5cd9905, with the specs, a runner and a smoke test in 9d33ca7 and this README, the help file and CI in dacc6a0.'),
    blank,
    ...text(r'What changed in the move is deliberately small, and the README lists it: the namespace (config.* became xyno_crates.*, xyno_rust.* and xyno_imports.*), setup() taking options, opt-in keys (the original bound <leader>rA and <leader>rG itself), switchable commands, a snacks check in place of an assumed global, and renamed identifiers (the in-process clients are xyno-crates and xyno-features, the diagnostic source is xyno-crates, the switch is vim.g.xyno_crate_check). Between 14 and 57 lines per module differ from the originals (counting both sides of a diff), out of 282, 997 and 2034. The logic is the logic that has been fixed and field-tested in xynovim since 2026-10-14.'),
    blank,
